{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"aperture aperture","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md","fileName":"Aperture.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Aperture","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Exposure and Lighting Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exposure and Lighting Forensics","Depth of Field","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"aperture aperture","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md","fileName":"Aperture.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Aperture","heading":"Aperture","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Aperture is the adjustable opening that controls how much light passes through a camera lens. A wider opening admits more light, while a narrower opening admits less and therefore requires compensation through shutter time, sensitivity, or scene illumination.\n\nAperture also influences [[Depth of Field]]. This makes it forensically useful: a recorded f-number can be compared with how quickly objects before and behind the focus distance become blurred, provided the analyst also considers focal length and subject distance.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exposure and Lighting Forensics","Depth of Field","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"aperture aperture","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Aperture.md","fileName":"Aperture.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Aperture","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","se